Subject: fix(tritium/core): register bindPeer on Linux too

Commit 5bd98514 guarded the Electron GUI sources with APPLE/WIN32 so the
headless Linux CI could build the core addon. The next day 49d6298c
("fix linux nodejs build") reverted that: the sources, the ElecView /
EcTimerImpl includes and the init_timer() / registerViewFactory() calls are
built on every platform again. Two guards were left behind, around the
bindPeer declaration in services.hpp and around its exports.Set() in
Init(). node_jsbr::bindPeer is therefore compiled into the Linux addon but
never exported, and the renderer worker's GfxManager.bindCanvas() fails with
"this.cuemol.bindPeer is not a function", leaving the 3D view black.

Remove the two leftover guards.

Apply with: git apply <this file>

diff --git a/tritium/core/cxx_src/init_cuemol.cpp b/tritium/core/cxx_src/init_cuemol.cpp
index 1a1d2969..b6e0d517 100644
--- a/tritium/core/cxx_src/init_cuemol.cpp
+++ b/tritium/core/cxx_src/init_cuemol.cpp
@@ -176,10 +176,8 @@ Napi::Object Init(Napi::Env env, Napi::Object exports)
     // exports.Set(Napi::String::New(env, "getClassName"),
     //             Napi::Function::New(env, node_jsbr::getClassName));
 
-#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(_WIN32)
     exports.Set(Napi::String::New(env, "bindPeer"),
                 Napi::Function::New(env, node_jsbr::bindPeer));
-#endif
 
     exports.Set(Napi::String::New(env, "copyFromTypedArray"),
                 Napi::Function::New(env, node_jsbr::copyFromTypedArray));
diff --git a/tritium/core/cxx_src/services.hpp b/tritium/core/cxx_src/services.hpp
index e6dd2905..7e8ec71f 100644
--- a/tritium/core/cxx_src/services.hpp
+++ b/tritium/core/cxx_src/services.hpp
@@ -9,9 +9,7 @@ Napi::Value createObj(const Napi::CallbackInfo &info);
 Napi::Value hasClass(const Napi::CallbackInfo &info);
 Napi::String getAllClassNamesJSON(const Napi::CallbackInfo &info);
 
-#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(_WIN32)
 Napi::Value bindPeer(const Napi::CallbackInfo &info);
-#endif
 
 /**
    Copy data from ByteArray to JS TypedArray
